title: task lock refs live inside the pushed refspec and can be published to the remote
updated: 2026-08-10T01:40:24Z
---

Found while fixing #86 and #45.

Locks are stored at refs/karr/tasks/N/lock, which is inside refs/karr/*, which is
what karr pushes. A lock is process-local state -- it means "this agent, in this
clone, is mid-pick right now" -- and it has no meaning in another clone.

After the #86 fix a lock is no longer held across the push on the success path,
so the common case is clean. But it is still structurally wrong: any sync that
fires while a lock is held publishes it, and then a lock taken by one clone
appears on the remote, gets pulled by others, and can only be cleared by the
new unlock command.

Fix direction: move locks out of refs/karr/* entirely -- e.g. refs/karr-local/*
-- so no refspec can reach them, rather than relying on the timing of when they
are released. That also removes them from backup/restore, where a snapshot
containing someone elses momentary lock is noise at best.

Check while doing it: the pull side prunes refs/karr/*, so a pruned lock and a
locally held lock must not be confused.
Fixed and merged into main (fa79722); full suite green at 93 files / 630 tests.
Reproduced before the fix, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix
code. #94 additionally confirmed empirically that libgit2 lookup-based delete
really does guard: moving the ref underneath it answers "old reference value
does not match".
